[[File:ADnD2e.png|300px|center|AD&D 2nd Edition]]
{{timeline|1989}}

== February ==
* Advanced Dungeons & Dragons 2nd Edition officially begins. Released are:
** {{dd|Player's Handbook (2e)|alt=Player's Handbook}}, referenced in:
*** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Campaign Setting|pdf=17267|nip=1}}
*** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Monstrous Compendium Appendix}}
*** {{b|Planescape|The Deva Spark|pdf=17271|nip=1}}

== May ==
** {{dd|Dungeon Master Guide (2e)|alt=Dungeon Master's Guide}}, referenced in:
*** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Campaign Setting|pdf=17267|nip=1}}
*** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Monstrous Compendium Appendix}}
*** {{b|Planescape|The Deva Spark|pdf=17271|nip=1}}

== June ==
* Released:
** {{dd|Monstrous Compendium Volume One|pdf=183092}}, referenced in:
*** {{b|D&D|Guide to Hell|pdf=17390}}

== October ==
* Released:
** {{b|Spelljammer|Spelljammer: Adventures in Space|pdf=17263|nip=1}}, D&D's first foray into a "meta-setting" that includes all other D&D worlds (albeit not [[Ravenloft]]).
** {{Dragonlance|Time of the Dragon|pdf=16960}}, referenced in:
*** {{b|Planescape|Planescape Monstrous Compendium Appendix}} (via {{b|Dragon|Dragon Magazine 218}})


